 have the medications supplies  and equipment and whatever other support  they may need over the weekend  so that there's no gap in service what i  appreciated most about  the way southwest medical runs their  volunteer program is  first of all  patients are a priority  number two  i need the tools or volunteer needs the  tools  to  put the patient's priorities first and  that came with training i absolutely  would encourage others to be involved in  hospice care if they want to chop  vegetables for  a nutrition session they might want to  do that or if they want to volunteer and  sit with the patient to give a family  member an opportunity to go grocery  shopping  or to go to an appointment or just a  respite two-hour session it's so  appreciated by the families by the  patients and it's so rewarding as a  volunteer  we want to say thank you again to  southwest medical for sponsoring this  segment and for being one of our  community pride partners  now let's
 

